Dear coaches,

Firstly, from our Team at Undiscovered World 48, we hope you has an amazing
experience in Dublin, Ireland and have now arrived home safely. It's was a
pleasure you have you come visit us in Ireland for this inaugural global
showcase event. The talent in the first year exceeded our own expectation
but as you can imagine we expect next year for this to eclipsed as the word
gets out about this year.

Personal I didn't get as much time as I'd like to get to know everyone of
you individually, but from the time I did get, I can't speak highly enough
of the quality of people I met across the board. If you are coming to
Ireland again outside of this event, I'm more then happy to help with
planning like arranging stays or pulling together a list of places to visit
or pulling a team together to play an exhibition/ pre-season game. I hope
you all "split a few G's and got a sense of the Irish hospitality we pride
ourselves on.

As coaches, you have been provided with the contact details of all players
attending so the ball is literally in your court now, but please reach out
to Brandon or George as your first points of contact for any other player
details required.

Some follow up items we want to share :

1. YouTube showcase game recordings :

World 48 | National Basketball Arena | Day 1
<https://youtube.com/live/Av8XUdiQUfo>
World 48 | National Basketball Arena | Day 2
<https://www.youtube.com/live/8a3QhjWJaDA?is=KEqeyFCaBxaJLCOd>

2. We want to make this the best event possible for next time so please
share the positives and areas were there are opportunities for us to
improve.

Feedback form
<https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1M_lvTI_ppfkeG0l0e2jNFoJvjDbxoGiD2YIujHO_0ZE/edit>


Thanks once again for making the trip to the event and hopefully see you
soon back on our green shamrock shores for an even longer stay -> the west
coast is the 8th wonder of the world !

Mark Reynolds & the Undiscovered World 48 Team

Email : mark.reynolds25@gmail.com | Phone :+353 4312417

[image: image.jpeg]

